  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "The parts are the same as in step 1; I found no error there.",
   "The circuit images never loaded, so the layout comes from the text. The text says three voltage dividers on analog pins A0, A1 and A2, each made of an analog sensor and a 10K resistor.",
   "I used FSRs as the sensors, since the text says the dividers are built from force-sensing resistors. A potentiometer or photocell would also fit the text.",
   "Each divider has the sensor from the 5V rail to a junction column, and the 10K resistor from that column to the GND rail. A jumper wire runs from the same column to the analog pin.",
   "Rail polarity is my assumption: top-plus rail (tp) is 5V and top-minus rail (tn) is GND. The Uno's 5V and GND.1 reach those rails through wire1 and wire2.",
   "Breadboard columns 5, 10 and 15 are my choice, and the sensor legs go straight into the rail holes. The sensors and resistors are not in the centre-gap style, so they sit in one half (top bank) only.",
   "The sensor-to-pin mapping is A0 for red, A1 for green and A2 for blue, as in the code."
  ]
 },
